# the Arzalluz report (AnCora CESS-CAST-P-20020801-17), into Italian.
# apertium-spa carries each with its paradigm and the bilingual pairs it
# with nothing: `mentir' is the verb `mienten' is, where the only verb spelt
# so was `mentar' in the subjunctive (they mention); `quejar' is `se
# quejó'; Spanish had no word for self-determination, nostalgic or
# Francoism. An English word is lower-case letters, so `self-determination'
# is never admitted and the word for it is `autodetermination'
<e><p><l>lie<s n="vblex"/></l><r>mentir<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
