# the Abogacía report (AnCora CESS-CAST-P-19991001-61), into Italian: each of
# these has its paradigm in apertium-spa.spa.dix and no English word, or one of
# several (`aprovechar' is `take advantage of'), and is only read (RL). An RL
# noun still comes before the dictionary's own further down the nouns, so the
# dictionary's `abogado' is said first, both ways, or `letrado' would be the
# first Spanish word for a lawyer; the Spanish words for procedure, stress and
# exploit stay the dictionary's as they come first (the verbs' RL entries come
# last). `honorario' is an honorarium, which is no `fee' (the dictionary's `fee'
# is a cost); `enjuiciamiento', as in `ley de enjuiciamiento civil', is the
# procedure
